        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospitalisation of your patient, a 69-year-old male, admitted on 11/09/2020 due to an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Diagnostic workup included arterial blood gas analysis, chest X-ray, blood tests, and pulse oximetry, confirming hypoxaemic respiratory failure consistent with COPD exacerbation. ECG showed no acute cardiac pathology. The patient was treated with supplemental oxygen therapy, inhaled bronchodilators via nebuliser, systemic corticosteroids, and intravenous fluids. Clinical response was satisfactory, with improvement in oxygenation and symptom relief. He was discharged on 12/09/2020 in stable condition. I recommend continuation of optimised inhaler therapy and close outpatient follow-up. Pulmonary rehabilitation referral has been advised. Please do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>"
            },
